    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <assignments>
        <description>Builds one Benefit record for the current loop iteration&#39;s Service Type and adds it to the create collection. Reuses the Service Type&#39;s own Unit of Measure.</description>
        <name>Build_Benefit_Record</name>
        <label>Build Benefit Record</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.Name</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Loop_Selected_Service_Types.Name</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.Name</assignToReference>
            <operator>Add</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue> - </stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.Name</assignToReference>
            <operator>Add</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Program.Name</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.BenefitTypeId</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Loop_Selected_Service_Types.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.ProgramId</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Program.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.IsActive</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.CanRegisterAsProvider</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>var_Benefit.UnitId</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Loop_Selected_Service_Types.UnitofMeasureId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>colBenefitsToCreate</assignToReference>
            <operator>Add</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>var_Benefit</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Selected_Service_Types</targetReference>
        </connector>
    </assignments>
    <decisions>
        <description>Short-circuits when the global master kill switch or this flow&#39;s own named-automation kill switch is active.</description>
        <name>Is_Kill_Switch_Active</name>
        <label>Is Kill Switch Active?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Kill_Switch_Message_Screen</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Kill Switch Active</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>All_Kill_Switches_Clear</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Setup.Global_Kill_Switch__c.Disable_All__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Setup.Automation_Kill_Switch__c.Disable_Program_Select_Service_Types__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Program</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>All Kill Switches Clear</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>DWDECI-119. Admin screen flow, callable as a subflow (e.g. from DWDECI-118&#39;s guided Program creation flow) or run directly against an existing Program: select active Service Types (BenefitType) from the master list and mass-generate child Benefit records for this one Program in a single bulk Create Records call (governor-limit safe for 200+ selections). Each Benefit reuses its Service Type&#39;s own Unit of Measure. SelectedServiceTypes (MultiSelectCheckboxes, valueField=Id) returns a semicolon-delimited raw string of Ids; Split_Selected_Service_Types (SplitStringInvocable Apex action) splits it into a real text collection before the Get_Selected_Service_Types lookup (filters on Id IN Split_Selected_Service_Types.values) - same confirmed platform quirk and fix as the Create &amp; Push flow. Fault paths -&gt; ErrorLogger.logFromFlow (ACC Base Utilities Log Error action). Gated by the global master kill switch and its own named-automation kill switch.</description>
    <dynamicChoiceSets>
        <name>ActiveServiceTypeChoices</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <displayField>Name</displayField>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Active__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>BenefitType</object>
        <sortField>Name</sortField>
        <sortOrder>Asc</sortOrder>
        <valueField>Id</valueField>
    </dynamicChoiceSets>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Program - Screen Flow - Select Service Types {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Program - Screen Flow - Select Service Types</label>
    <loops>
        <description>Iterates every selected Service Type to build one child Benefit per Service Type for this Program.</description>
        <name>Loop_Selected_Service_Types</name>
        <label>Loop Selected Service Types</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <collectionReference>Get_Selected_Service_Types</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Build_Benefit_Record</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
        <noMoreValuesConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Benefits</targetReference>
        </noMoreValuesConnector>
    </loops>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>Flow</processType>
    <recordCreates>
        <description>Single bulk create of every child Benefit (no DML in the loop). Governor-limit safe for 200+ selected Service Types.</description>
        <name>Create_Benefits</name>
        <label>Create Benefits</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <faultConnector>
            <targetReference>Log_Error_Create_Benefits</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <inputReference>colBenefitsToCreate</inputReference>
    </recordCreates>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Gets the Program (Id and Name) the flow is running against, from the recordId input.</description>
        <name>Get_Program</name>
        <label>Get Program</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Select_Service_Types_Screen</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <faultConnector>
            <targetReference>Log_Error_Get_Program</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>recordId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Program</object>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
        <queriedFields>Name</queriedFields>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <description>Gets the full BenefitType records (Id, Name, UnitofMeasureId) for whatever was selected on screen, to build each child Benefit.</description>
        <name>Get_Selected_Service_Types</name>
        <label>Get Selected Service Types</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Selected_Service_Types</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <faultConnector>
            <targetReference>Log_Error_Get_Selected_Service_Types</targetReference>
        </faultConnector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>In</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Split_Selected_Service_Types.values</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>false</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>BenefitType</object>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
        <queriedFields>Name</queriedFields>
        <queriedFields>UnitofMeasureId</queriedFields>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
